---
title: "Table"
description: "Readable tables, with optional borders, zebra rows and sortable columns."
tags: [data, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  Base styles apply to every `<table>`. Add the `table` class for borders and
  zebra rows. To make a column sortable, give its `<th>` `aria-sort="none"` and a
  `<button>` inside, then call `initTables()`:

  ```js
  import { initTables } from "./table.js";

  initTables(); // or initTables(root, ".table")
  ```

  Sorting compares cell text, with numbers in numeric order.
accessibility: |
  - Give every table a `<caption>`, and use `<th scope="col">` and
    `<th scope="row">` for headers.
  - Wrap wide tables in an element with `tabindex="0"`, `role="region"` and a
    label, so keyboard users can scroll them on small screens.
  - `aria-sort` on the sorted header is updated to `ascending` or `descending`,
    and screen readers announce it.
customProperties:
  "--table-cell-padding": "Padding of every cell."
  "--table-caption-gap": "Space between the caption and the table."
  "--table-border-color": "Color of the row borders."
  "--table-head-border": "Border under the header row."
  "--table-stripe": "Background of every other row."
  "--table-focus-ring": "Outline of the focused scroll container."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<h3>Standard table</h3>

<div class="table-wrapper" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Browser support">
<table>
  <caption>Browser support</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Feature</th>
      <th scope="col">Chrome</th>
      <th scope="col">Firefox</th>
      <th scope="col">Safari</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Popover</th><td>114</td><td>125</td><td>17</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">@scope</th><td>118</td><td>146</td><td>17.4</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">dialog</th><td>37</td><td>98</td><td>15.4</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Sortable table</h3>

<div class="table-wrapper" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Components">
  <table class="table">
    <caption>Components</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col" aria-sort="none"><button type="button">Name</button></th>
        <th scope="col" aria-sort="none"><button type="button">Type</button></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Tabs</td><td>Navigation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Alert</td><td>Feedback</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Card</td><td>Layout</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<script type="module">
  import { initTables } from "./table.js";

  initTables();
</script>
